{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "pw8-fx-fractal-morph",
    "name": "FX FRACTAL MORPH",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "A slow, sustained saw pad through FractalEcho -- this project's own invented FX algorithm (docs/FX_BANK.md 'The invented algorithm'), not modeled on any researched plugin. Instead of a manually patched delay tree, FractalEcho procedurally generates a small self-similar 6-node delay tree from a 64-bit seed (deeper nodes get proportionally shorter, self-similar delay times), and continuously morphs between TWO such generated topologies (seedA=101, seedB=909) via a single `fractalMorph` parameter -- interpolated in COEFFICIENT space at audio rate, not a signal-domain crossfade. This preset parks morph at a fixed 0.35 (a static snapshot partway between the two topologies); a host with per-parameter automation could sweep it live to hear the whole delay network's rhythm and stereo image continuously reshape, not just its wet/dry balance.",
    "category": "pad",
    "moods": [
      "evolving",
      "spacious",
      "otherworldly"
    ],
